{
  "headline": "Pump.fun's GO Bounty Feature Sparks Outrage Over Dangerous Stunts",
  "facts": [
    "Pump.fun launched its GO bounty feature in early June 2026 with the tagline 'Pay ANYONE to do ANYTHING'",
    "The platform has paid out over $370,000 since June 4, 2026",
    "Approximately 270 open bounties remain with more than $200,000 in unclaimed rewards",
    "A man in the Philippines received $15,000 in crypto for tattooing 'bounty.fun' on his forehead",
    "The highest-value bounty offers $57,200 for climbing Mount Everest and placing a bet on Howl.com",
    "Other tasks have included quitting jobs on camera ($3,100), wearing a gorilla suit in public ($322), and dumping milk on oneself while shouting a cryptocurrency name ($72)",
    "New York Governor Kathy Hochul called the platform a 'dystopian nightmare' and offered a bounty on the first bill to ban it",
    "X head of product Nikita Bier criticized the feature, saying 'rich people left crypto and now teenagers force poor people to do shameful things'",
    "GO gives Pump.fun sole authority to accept or reject tasks and submissions",
    "Pump.fun previously shut down livestreaming after users engaged in extreme behavior; it later returned with stricter moderation"
  ],
  "quotes": [
    {
      "text": "Humans & money are undeniably the most powerful tools on Earth. We're combining both of them with GO: an all encompassing bounty platform where ANYONE can create or complete bounties for ANY task for UNLIMITED rewards.",
      "attribution": "Pump.fun, X post (as reported by NY Post)"
    },
    {
      "text": "Offering a bounty on the first bill introduced to ban this dystopian nightmare",
      "attribution": "NY Governor Kathy Hochul, X post"
    },
    {
      "text": "It's sad that all the rich people left crypto and it's now the entire industry is just teenagers in America forcing poor people to do shameful things",
      "attribution": "Nikita Bier, X head of product"
    },
    {
      "text": "This is essentially what the digital economy is boiling down to",
      "attribution": "Andrew Ford Lyons, technologist, to WIRED"
    }
  ],
  "analysis": "For memecoin traders, this story highlights a critical inflection point for Pump.fun—one of Solana's most influential meme coin launchpads. The GO feature controversy could attract regulatory scrutiny that impacts the entire ecosystem. New York Governor Hochul's public condemnation signals potential legislative action that could cascade to other jurisdictions. The platform's ability to moderate and self-regulate will be tested. If Pump.fun faces shutdowns or severe restrictions, it could disrupt the Solana meme coin market significantly. Traders should monitor: (1) any official regulatory responses beyond political statements, (2) whether Pump.fun announces moderation policy changes, and (3) user migration to alternative platforms. The timing is notable—GO launched as Pump.fun contended with an 80% crash in user engagement, suggesting desperation for new revenue streams.",
  "source_urls": [
    "https://crypto.news/pump-funs-bounty-feature-faces-backlash-over-risky-crypto-tasks/",
    "https://nypost.com/2026/06/20/world-news/bizarre-bounty-site-has-desperate-risk-takers-tattooing-their-foreheads-climbing-mount-everest-for-crypto/",
